# Project memory maintenance

`PROJECT_MEMORY.md` at the repository root is the canonical architecture and feature tracker for MMR.

## When to update

At the **end of every user prompt** where you made progress (code, design, debugging, or decisions), update `PROJECT_MEMORY.md` before finishing your reply.

Skip only when the turn was purely informational with **no** project state change (e.g. a one-line clarification) and nothing new belongs in the memory file.

## What to record

- New or changed features, UX contracts, and user-visible behavior
- Schema / Room version bumps, migrations, backup format changes
- Important algorithms (interest accrual, SMS rules, approval flow)
- Key file paths for new subsystems
- Known test/build caveats (failing suites, required flags)

## How to update

- Prefer **editing existing sections** (§5 Development Roadmap, §6 Key Implementation Decisions, §7 Current State) over duplicating bullets.
- Use dated subsections when a large area grows (e.g. `### Loans`).
- Keep §8 Maintenance Note accurate; do not claim the file is never auto-updated.
- Do **not** commit unless the user asked for a commit.

## Completion check

Before sending the final message, confirm `PROJECT_MEMORY.md` reflects work done in **this** turn and any still-relevant context from the session.
